nfig.mjs:78`). |\n\n\nThis asymmetry is deliberate. The block lands *inside* `CLAUDE.md`, next to\nhand-written instructions, and a tracked file cannot be half-ignored — so the\nchoice was between committing it or having `CLAUDE.md` read as permanently\nmodified in every checkout. Committing it wins; the cost is churn when the graph\nis reindexed and the symbol counts shift.\n\nThe standalone files are a different case: they are nothing *but* generated\noutput, so ignoring them loses no hand-written content. The `.gitignore` comment\nspells this out so the next reader does not \"fix\" the inconsistency.\n\n\n- The ignore rules are deliberately narrow — `/.claude/skills/generated/` does\n  not shadow the tracked `.claude/agents/`, verified with `git check-ignore`.\n- If `.github/copilot-instructions.md` or `AGENTS.md` ever grows real\n  hand-written content, drop its ignore rule; the comment in `.gitignore` says so.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}